results.task:
You are the SPRINT BOUNDARY crew - ONE mechanical child, NOT a planner and NOT an implementer. Do exactly the parts below and nothing else. Do NOT remove any worktree or branch.
PART 2 - BD SNAPSHOT (read-only). Report EVERY leaf of bd epic "pi-autoresearch-ee7" (children with no children of their own).
Run these commands with piped stdin (read-only; do NOT create, close or modify anything in bd):
  (a) bd list --parent pi-autoresearch-ee7 --all -n 0 --json </dev/null   - the epic's children (JSON array: id, title, status)
  (b) bd show <ALL child ids from (a), space-separated> --json </dev/null   - ONE call, JSON array with description and dependencies[]
  (c) ONE bash for-loop: for i in <child ids>; do bd list --parent "$i" --all -n 0 --json </dev/null; done   - a child with a non-empty result has children of its own: it is NOT a leaf, omit it
Map each leaf exactly:
  id = id; title = title; open = (status != "closed");
  rationale = description, first 300 chars;
  acceptance = the test/contract clause of the description (the sentence that states the tests or contract), first 300 chars, '' if none;
  files_hint = the first file path named in the description, first 200 chars, '' if none;
  measure = the value of the "Метод измерения:" line of the description (the whole line after the colon, first 200 chars), '' if the line is absent - the engine needs it to issue a visual-criterion leaf into work (П6);
  deps = ids of dependencies[] entries whose dependency_type is "blocks" (parent-child entries are NOT deps), [] if none;
  review = the tier word full|lite|none that the description states for the task; missing or unknown -> "full".
Return only leaves shown by (a)-(c); NEVER invent ids.
FINAL MESSAGE DISCIPLINE: your final message must be ONLY the JSON value with EXACTLY the schema keys listed in your instructions. Do NOT emit acceptanceReport or any other key; narrative goes inside string fields.

Schema keys: closed[{id, closed (boolean), note}] (omit when there is no BD CLOSE section), leaves[{id, title, rationale, acceptance, files_hint, measure, deps, open, review}].

